    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8dddf5f_3f816fa6",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-23T21:10:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The changes here are needed to support FIFO reads via I2C. The proposed method relies on the burstcount field within the STS register to handshake with the Host so that it can extract enough of the message header to calculate the total message length. After the first read, then the burstcount field needs to be set back to the maximum or nominal value. That\u0027s why there\u0027s a check to see if it\u0027s the first FIFO read.\n\nI did not modify this section from the original patch, but the modifications seem correct to me.",
      "parentUuid": "3e3be95b_c9942993",
      "revId": "affddff1e75ef126cc719abd3e8f1e95c61d2822",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
